    "created_at": "2022-02-09T22:57:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-09T22:57:30Z",
    "body": "Unfortunately from an implementation perspective scoping this feature request down to a session-specific device identifier that survives the device being reconnected doesn't make the problem any simpler than creating an identifier that is persistent between sessions. Today, if the device isn't disconnected then `getDevices()` and `requestDevice()` will return `HIDDevice` instances that are `===` comparable to each other. Difficulty occurs when the device is disconnected and the browser needs to decide that the device that the OS told it got disconnected before is the same as the device the OS told it just connected and give it the same identifier.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
