    "created_at": "2022-07-07T16:02:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-07T16:02:06Z",
    "body": "> Unfortunately from an implementation perspective scoping this feature request down to a session-specific device identifier that survives the device being reconnected doesn't make the problem any simpler than creating an identifier that is persistent between sessions.\r\n\r\nWould it at least be possible to provide a unique session id per device that does _not_ survive a disconnect event?  Anything at this point would be welcome.  \r\n\r\n",
